Teach the standalone generator to emit BF16 x BF16 -> F32 dense GEMMs.

The CLI only accepted SP, DP and I16, so add a BF16F32 precision (A and B in
BF16, C and compute in F32) and a BF16F32_VNNI_A one that also sets
LIBXSMM_GEMM_FLAG_VNNI_A, so A comes pre-packed in K pairs. Give the
inline-assembly emitter a C signature for them, and fix the text emitter for
the instructions LIBXSMM's BF16 CPX kernels use, which until now only the JIT
encoder had exercised:

- vmovdqu16, vpunpck{l,h}wd, vshufi64x2 and vinserti32x8 had no mnemonic, so
  an uninitialised buffer was printed in their place;
- vinserti32x8 (and the other 256-bit inserts) printed the inserted operand as
  a zmm instead of a ymm;
- kmov{b,w,d} from a legacy GPR printed a NUL byte for the missing `d` suffix
  and the 64-bit register name, e.g. `kmovd %rbx`; it now prints `%ebx`;
- vdpbf16ps with a broadcast memory operand, which the VNNI kernel issues for
  an M block of one vector, printed `{1to8}`, a qword broadcast; its operand
  is a BF16 pair, so it now prints `{1to16}`.

SP and DP output is byte-identical.

